// A runtime error names the line of its statement, also after a block that
// created a variable.
//
// The VM's compiler cleared the block's variables with instructions that skipped
// the table of source positions, and from there on every instruction carried the
// position of the one after it: this division reported line 16, the `>>`
// (BUG-VMJS-004, found by the JavaScript port of the VM). The consensus compares
// the `-->` line across the engines; a golden cannot, it drops it.

x = 0
? x == 0 {
    y = 1
    >> y ¶
}
z = 5 / x
>> z x ¶
